{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character","id":1022973,"title":"The Beast as a Player Character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-27T14:56:00-08:00","id":1022973,"title":"The Beast as a Player Character","content":"Running of a suggestion in the 2e corebook I'm going to be implementing that each player will be responsible for playing another PC's Beast.<br /> I think it sounds extremely interesting and like something that can both increase the drama as well as a method for each character to gain the spotlight - even without the ST passing the baton, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I'm curious as to whether or not any of you have any experience with this method, and what those experiences may be?<br /> <br /> What techniques did you use?<br /> What guidelines did you give the players beforehand?<br /> How did your players feel about this style of play?<br /> How did this addition affect the game?<br /> <br /> I have a bunch of questions, so it's probably best if I hold back and keep it to the questions above and whatever else you may feel is relevant to share <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm currently considering a couple of things, including the Beast as a narrative player devise or an approach with a seperate character sheet for the Beast (adding dots to certain abilities, attributes etc. while the Beast has control) and certain clan-specific abilities that help underline why each clan is perceived to be they way they are or be able to do some of the things they are rumored to do. <br /> But I'd like to hear what you guys have to say before I put too much (or too little) effort into this trail of thought <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:05:48-08:00","id":1022984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkeyMann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character#post1022973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running of a suggestion in the 2e corebook I'm going to be implementing that each player will be responsible for playing another PC's Beast.<br /> I think it sounds extremely interesting and like something that can both increase the drama as well as a method for each character to gain the spotlight - even without the ST passing the baton, so to speak.<br /> <br /> I'm curious as to whether or not any of you have any experience with this method, and what those experiences may be?<br /> <br /> What techniques did you use?<br /> What guidelines did you give the players beforehand?<br /> How did your players feel about this style of play?<br /> How did this addition affect the game?<br /> <br /> I have a bunch of questions, so it's probably best if I hold back and keep it to the questions above and whatever else you may feel is relevant to share <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm currently considering a couple of things, including the Beast as a narrative player devise or an approach with a seperate character sheet for the Beast (adding dots to certain abilities, attributes etc. while the Beast has control) and certain clan-specific abilities that help underline why each clan is perceived to be they way they are or be able to do some of the things they are rumored to do.<br /> But I'd like to hear what you guys have to say before I put too much (or too little) effort into this trail of thought <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is not something I have heard of at all. I have always thought the beast was a more primal instinct rather than an actual person who can talk and have conversations. The book references many times over the beast only wants 1 of 3 things. Feed, Flee or Kill. <br /> <br /> You would more or less be rewriting the entire game as is. Though if you really want to do it, treat it more like a possession, like a strix?<br /> <br /> The beast already gives you BP bonus to all physicals while it's in control, therefore it would give it to all the skills you try to use with those. Like brawl or running away...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:18:45-08:00","id":1022990,"title":"","content":"Be careful about giving control of one player's character to another player. If your group is fine with someone else role playing their character when that person is temporarily absent it may be okay, but taking away player agency is a touchy issue between ST and player. So I expect it'd be exacerbated with players doing it.<br /> <br /> I got to watch a Wraith chronicle fall apart a long time ago in a similar scenario and can tell a few horror stories about what happened when players got control of other players' characters. I suppose it depends on the group but I personally would be unlikely to play in a game where other people arbitrarily get to seize control my character's actions and development without my input because the GM has a taste for out of game melodrama.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:23:44-08:00","id":1022994,"title":"","content":"I read it as an optional rule somewhere, and found it interesting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Now having it as someone you talk to hasn't been a part of my thoughts thus far. I'm currently leaning more toward the other player describing feelings and trying to nudge the character to do something that aligns with the Beast's nature <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> It would seem that I have a different reading on the Beast than you do. Who knows? Maybe I'm wrong. Hehe.<br /> But the &quot;possession&quot; rute is a valid suggestion. So thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T15:32:16-08:00","id":1022999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1022990#post1022990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Be careful about giving control of one player's character to another player. If your group is fine with someone else role playing their character when that person is temporarily absent it may be okay, but taking away player agency is a touchy issue between ST and player. So I expect it'd be exacerbated with players doing it.<br /> <br /> I got to watch a Wraith chronicle fall apart a long time ago in a similar scenario and can tell a few horror stories about what happened when players got control of other players' characters. I suppose it depends on the group but I personally would be unlikely to play in a game where other people arbitrarily get to seize control my character's actions and development without my input because the GM has a taste for out of game melodrama.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair point. Perhaps I should explain. I don't see this as &quot;Out of game melodrama&quot; at all. In fact I see it as a firmly in game thing. The Beast isn't something you control. And it's something that's ever present. Having another player control it during a frenzy is not really different than having the ST control it in that situation. But in reality the Frenzy is a somewhat rare thing (at least at our table), and so more often than not the way this &quot;mechanic&quot; would present is by one player being the &quot;devil on your shoulder&quot; to another player. That's the way I picture it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> But I respect your oppinion and experience, and will take it into consideration <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T16:18:42-08:00","id":1023020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1022984#post1022984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not something I have heard of at all. I have always thought the beast was a more primal instinct rather than an actual person who can talk and have conversations. The book references many times over the beast only wants 1 of 3 things. Feed, Flee or Kill.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's one of the alternate rule ideas from the storytelling chapter. Page 278, under Twist: Beast Guides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1022984#post1022984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would more or less be rewriting the entire game as is. Though if you really want to do it, treat it more like a possession, like a strix?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's definitely not my cup of tea. I very much prefer the Beast to be the vampires own uninhibited base urges (as per the default) than as an intelligent alien consciousness. But, to each their own I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1022984#post1022984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The beast already gives you BP bonus to all physicals while it's in control, therefore it would give it to all the skills you try to use with those. Like brawl or running away...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, a separate character sheet for the Beast seems like a very strange choice to me too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T16:31:15-08:00","id":1023022,"title":"","content":"I've always had the Beast as a more palpable thing, but never this much. Like a dark voice inside the player can use to embellish their descriptions or I can to get across how a vampire might feel about a certain situation.<br /> <br /> It's the kind of thing that seems to work in Wraith, with their spectres, but the spectres are a more individualistic and unique character, even as much as they are part of the PC.<br /> <br /> I forget which book, whether it's the Chronicler's Guide or Danse Macabre, but it introduces 'The Other' as an optional variant to the Beast. Rather than the Beast's fiery-eyed predator, the Other is a cold, detatched presence.<br /> <br /> A section in upcoming supplements detailing and offering options for the Beast would be really cool, as the whole Predatory Aura seems to have expanded on that. I don't think it would be worth having a different player play, but the Beast is certainly something that should be explored in-game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:50:07-08:00","id":1023049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkeyMann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1022999#post1022999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't see this as &quot;Out of game melodrama&quot; at all. In fact I see it as a firmly in game thing. The Beast isn't something you control. And it's something that's ever present. Having another player control it during a frenzy is not really different than having the ST control it in that situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things about this though<br /> 1. It's been my experience that when a character succumbs to frenzy or the character becomes mind controlled, the ST (or other PC) still doesn't take control of the character. (I've only seen it on three specific occasions and that was at the player's express request.) That character's player retains control, it's a matter of the player keeping in mind that another sentience is the one declaring the actions in broad strokes and they are the one providing the details. If the player still acts in a manner deemed &quot;out of character&quot; for the circumstances, that is when the ST intervenes. <br /> 2. It's different because the ST is more likely to simply have the character act simply to keep the game going whereas another player is likely to use the opportunity to sabotage the temporarily controlled character out of spite for another incident, use the circumstances to directly advance their own character or agendas or do the same thing you'd typically take control from the player for doing, and that's behave in an uncharacteristic manner to avoid too much potential collateral damage to the group or individual.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying don't do it, I'm advising to be careful about how it's handled. I would suggest some sort of ground rules on what sort of actions are permitted or forbidden by players who don't own the character and don't have to take responsibility for their choices.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T18:33:57-08:00","id":1023058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1023049#post1023049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. It's different because the ST is more likely to simply have the character act simply to keep the game going whereas another player is likely to use the opportunity to sabotage the temporarily controlled character out of spite for another incident, use the circumstances to directly advance their own character or agendas or do the same thing you'd typically take control from the player for doing, and that's behave in an uncharacteristic manner to avoid too much potential collateral damage to the group or individual.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying don't do it, I'm advising to be careful about how it's handled. I would suggest some sort of ground rules on what sort of actions are permitted or forbidden by players who don't own the character and don't have to take responsibility for their choices.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the biggest thing to keep in mind when allowing other players to control another's PC. I won't go so far as to say it's likely a player will sabotage another PC out of spite, but it is possible as some experiences can attest.<br /> <br /> Not that you shouldn't go ahead with this idea, but it's something to keep in mind when GMing things: if you see anybody acting in a way that's just being an asshole as opposed to being in-character, don't be afraid to pull them into line very, very quickly, telling them your expectations. Your minimum expectation should be that the players should all respect one another and their 'property' enough not to ruin another player's fun. Basically, the players should take their duty as a Beast with the same seriousness and care you'd expect from a GM judging a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T06:41:40-08:00","id":1023241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1023058#post1023058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the biggest thing to keep in mind when allowing other players to control another's PC. I won't go so far as to say it's likely a player will sabotage another PC out of spite, but it is possible as some experiences can attest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd caution against this idea of players controlling beasts if only for something like this. Because it doesn't even matter if sabotage occurs, but I see it as a pretty easy way to bring up some unnecessary animosity. Maybe you have a really mature group. However, I can easily see people getting more upset that another player guided their frenzying beast into a negative course of action than the ST doing it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T07:34:54-08:00","id":1023265,"title":"","content":"*Some* groups could do it well. It'd require a sit down talk first. Set the expectation of the player controlling the Beast making the PC's life hell as much as possible and make sure that there will be no ooc Feels.<br /> <br /> Also shut down using beast time to forward your character's goals.<br /> <br /> After the first time it happens talk to your players again about it to make sure its still okay.<br /> <br /> I would also sidebar anyone who it happens to privately after the game and I would reinforce both good beast plays *and* accepting those plays with praise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T08:37:13-08:00","id":1023294,"title":"","content":"One thing i'm experiencing with in my current game, is giving each player a 'dark aspiration' that represent what each characters beast wants. I tell the players that accomplishing these aspirations will trigger an degeneration roll but earn them a beat as per the regular aspiration rule. Whether they go for it or not i leave it entirely in the players choice.<br /> What that does for me is that the beast is still there even beyond frenzy rolls. That there is always these small thoughts nagging at the back of the characters head. It makes the beast a subtle thing but still there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T09:13:33-08:00","id":1023305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1023020#post1023020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one of the alternate rule ideas from the storytelling chapter. Page 278, under Twist: Beast Guides.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div> So it is <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I read over a bunch of the alternate rules way way back and decided I didn't like them, clearly this was one that was purged from Memory. <br /> <br /> <br /> As far as what the other's are saying, I would also recommend being super careful with your group and letting players take control of other player's character's. There is already so much backstabbing and whatnot in vampire, that it would be hard to control another player's character without some sort of Bias toward yours. I mean what if your character is the one that provoked the frenzy? You would have a hard time trying to kill your own character?<br /> What if the player took Ride the wave?<br /> <br /> I even got a little PO'd at my story teller for taking away a little control recently. We were fighting a big baddy and It was about to light some huge fire. And I was low on vitae. I asked her if this was enough to frenzy and kill it. like kill or be killed sort of thing. I knew if it lit the fire, I would die, but I knew if I hit it hard enough it would die and not light the fire... So she said ok, frenzy. then made me fear frenzy and run away. It seemed counter productive to the whole thing..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T15:01:18-08:00","id":1023446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1023305#post1023305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is already so much backstabbing and whatnot in vampire, that it would be hard to control another player's character without some sort of Bias toward yours. I mean what if your character is the one that provoked the frenzy? You would have a hard time trying to kill your own character?</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case i would either take control of the character myself or have one of the players not present in the scene take control, as to limit the bias.<br /> However - although I'm loathe to admit this - I would, as would any other ST (I suspect), be somewhat biased myself in regard to what would further the story most in that scene. And in that regard the storyteller is not much better than another player, in regard to that verdict being a very subjective point of view. After all, what futhers the storyteller agenda may not always be what furthers the story - as per the player perspective. And may, as such, be as counter productive as if another player had played with his or her bias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3448-monkeymann","name":"MonkeyMann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:09:46-08:00","id":1023800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MonkeyMann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1023446#post1023446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this case i would either take control of the character myself or have one of the players not present in the scene take control, as to limit the bias.<br /> However - although I'm loathe to admit this - I would, as would any other ST (I suspect), be somewhat biased myself in regard to what would further the story most in that scene. And in that regard the storyteller is not much better than another player, in regard to that verdict being a very subjective point of view. After all, what futhers the storyteller agenda may not always be what furthers the story - as per the player perspective. And may, as such, be as counter productive as if another player had played with his or her bias.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which is why I personally let my players do what they want (to a degree) in a frenzy. I don't do much more than, &quot;Your in a kill frenzy, Go&quot; They usually do just fine going all nutz and trying to kill. Or feed or run, if that's the frenzy they are in. They have no agenda to wreck the story, and well, They are the story, It wraps around them, so if they do something totally off the wall in a frenzy, We just adjust and it can make for some very interesting aftermath. If they destroy themselves, they have no one to blame, but if the story teller or another player took away control and the character was destroyed in someway ( not just death ) it would leave a bitter taste in the player's mouth. Just a warning from a lot of us here, bitter players aren't fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T14:23:34-08:00","id":1023940,"title":"","content":"As a former Wraith Player/Storyteller and Giest Storyteller, I like the idea of &quot;Guides&quot; to handle the tempting/corrupting storytelling workload. 2nd Edition seems well suited to it, especially vampire with the Beast-Defining Merits, Lashing out with the Beast, nuanced rules for Riding the Wave, and Conditions. Shadow Guides from Wraith (Spectres being Wraiths ruled by their Shadows instead of their Psyche) carrot approach might be well adapted 2nd Conditions that other players give a Character when that character leans on certain Beast powers, I envision<br /> <br /> Tempted to: ______________<br /> The whispering of the Beast has lodged a thought in your head, and while you could deny the temptation, it'd feel so good to indulge it. Regain a Willpower Point in addition to gaining a Beat when Resolving this Condition. (this is essentially a Temporary Vice and acts as such)<br /> Resolution: Give in to the temptation written on this Condition<br /> <br /> Also as a recovering LARPer I'd want some type of physical representation of the each beast's nature, possible in the form of a Concept Phrase or Image to act as inspiration for the Guide so they can understand the player of the character original intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-29-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T08:03:29-08:00","id":1025072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1022973-the-beast-as-a-player-character?p=1023940#post1023940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a former Wraith Player/Storyteller and Giest Storyteller, I like the idea of &quot;Guides&quot; to handle the tempting/corrupting storytelling workload. 2nd Edition seems well suited to it, especially vampire with the Beast-Defining Merits, Lashing out with the Beast, nuanced rules for Riding the Wave, and Conditions. Shadow Guides from Wraith (Spectres being Wraiths ruled by their Shadows instead of their Psyche) carrot approach might be well adapted 2nd Conditions that other players give a Character when that character leans on certain Beast powers, I envision<br /> <br /> Tempted to: ______________<br /> The whispering of the Beast has lodged a thought in your head, and while you could deny the temptation, it'd feel so good to indulge it. Regain a Willpower Point in addition to gaining a Beat when Resolving this Condition. (this is essentially a Temporary Vice and acts as such)<br /> Resolution: Give in to the temptation written on this Condition</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea. You can give each player one card per session that they can write down a temptation and give to another player. It'd definitely fit your idea of a little 'devil on the shoulder', especially with a Beat on offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T11:47:40-08:00","id":1026087,"title":"","content":"If the point is &quot;controlling the actions of a character under frenzy&quot; then there's going to be trouble. You could use Pale_Crusader's card method to influence through the beat system, which is what it's there for after all. That would get everyone involved and you could limit how many cards each player gets to tempt others with based on how many times they succumbed, took a dramatic failure or whatever. <br /> <br /> Another method, albeit an awkward one since you need an &quot;extra&quot; player, is to take a &quot;Storyteller's helper&quot; and assign him or her to play all beasts. It's tricky, but I played an analogous role in an old d6 Star Wars campaign once, tempting players toward the Dark Side with gratuitous rewards. I was also playing a key antagonist in parallel sessions with the GM, but that's what you get for stepping into a game &quot;late&quot;. It all worked very well, ultimately, though I'm sure the therapy bills were higher.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}